From b660e216a3fcfc5bcf517413ab15b9c934254dd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:50:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Regulatory-cassette framework: auditor-insertable lenses with
 chain-native insertion and disclosure events

A regulatory cassette is a LENS, not policy: it reviews decisions
against one regulation's expectations and flags for human review.
Own contract, registry, identity namespace (regulatory:name:version),
and directory -- structurally impossible to load as domain policy.

- regulatory_cassette_interface: lens ABC (observer/live mode
  manifest), findings, decision-material adapters (episode + ledger
  row; actor_report never enters), fail-loud validation, separate
  registry, screening-not-certification disclaimer on every report.
- regulatory_checks: regulation-parameterized checkers -- adverse-
  action reason specificity (deterministic scoring, evidence shows
  phrase hits + case references) and prohibited-basis/proxy input
  screen (declared-name only; statistical disparate-impact
  deliberately deferred).
- regulatory_deck: insertion binds lens content hash through the
  existing bind_cassette_version tripwire, writes first-class
  regulatory_cassette_inserted/removed events; live path disclosure-
  first -- every flag/block written to the chain naming regulation
  and check BEFORE it takes effect, failed disclosure aborts the
  action (no silent path). explain() reports without writing.
- ledger: three new hash-chained record kinds with matching
  reconstruction branches in verify_chain AND twin_custody (shared
  canonical_fields contract; no new columns, no parallel log).
  get_regulatory_cassette_history = the examiner query.
- regulatory_cassettes/cfpb_reg_b: CFPB / ECOA / Reg B reference
  lens; everything regulation-specific is profile DATA. CMS-style
  reuse proven in tests through the unmodified checker.
- forensics: the three new modules join _GOVERNANCE_CODE_MODULES;
  consequently ivr + banking bump 2.0.0 -> 2.0.1 (moved code hash
  requires a new version under binding enforcement; behavior
  unchanged) with test pins updated.
- READMEs: regulatory_cassettes/ (framework) + cassettes/ (domain
  module; closes one of the six missing module READMEs).
- Tests/test_regulatory_cassettes.py: 34 tests against live
  Postgres -- interface fail-closed, chain+twin verification of all
  three event kinds, binding tripwire on altered lens config,
  observer review writes nothing, disclosure-before-effect,
  disclosure-failure aborts, checker parameterization, proxy screen,
  forensics surface coverage.

Suite: 341 passed (307 baseline + 34 new), real PostgreSQL.
